 orders about 15% too much of both products (568 / 859). It also nearly fills the warehouse on day 11 (about 192 of 200). The surplus costs more than the shortages it prevents.\n- **3:** orders about 4.6% below the mean (473 / 715). That loses moderately on shortages.\n- **5:** orders about 9% below the mean (450 / 679). It is the worst on shortages.\n- **4:** orders every 4 days, which saves about 116 on order fees, and its quantities are at the mean. But leftover product 0 can't carry over to the next delivery. On day 9 the warehouse overflows: about 49 units of product 0 + 150 of product 1 + leftovers, more than 200. Overall it is roughly neutral.\n- **2 and 6:** quantities at the mean, but 13 order days instead of 9 cost about 232 more. Ordering more often matches demand slightly better and wins back part of that.\n\nMy rough order: 7 ≈ 0 > 4 > 2 > 6 ≈ 3 > 1 > 5."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5066, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5066}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:28:51.807Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWDDjmgEzL9Pgp9hVFcc"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01HiSbea5mAquV82cuWQELjT", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWDDk1ZrhQnqzXuWUw6M", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01H